|The indicator represents land use change from agriculture to artificial surfaces between 2000 and 2018 in absolute terms (hectares) and as a percentage of the agricultural area in 2000 (100 m grid, NUTS 3 regions or country level). Land use change is defined as the exits from agricultural land use broken down by non – agricultural sectors. It represents the conversion of agricultural area to non-agricultural use.CORINE Land Cover accounting layer 2000 and 2018 has been used as input data.|The indicator represents land use change from agriculture to artificial surfaces between 2000 and 2018 in absolute terms (hectares) and as a percentage of the agricultural area in 2000 (100 m grid, NUTS 3 regions or country level). Land use change is defined as the exits from agricultural land use broken down by non – agricultural sectors. It represents the conversion of agricultural area to non-agricultural use.CORINE Land Cover accounting layer 2000 and 2018 has been used as input data.|The indicator represents land use change from agriculture to artificial surfaces between 2000 and 2018 in absolute terms (hectares) and as a percentage of the agricultural area in 2000 (100 m grid, NUTS 3 regions or country level). Land use change is defined as the exits from agricultural land use broken down by non – agricultural sectors. It represents the conversion of agricultural area to non-agricultural use.CORINE Land Cover accounting layer 2000 and 2018 has been used as input data.|
