|The objective of EEA was to estimate the likelihood of presence of HNV farmland within Europe using existing European-wide datasets. The CLC European dataset was used as it was available consistently across the great majority of European countries. It was, though, noted that these data have several drawbacks related to geometric limitations (minimum mapping unit [MMU] of 25 ha), thematic resolution (particular class assessment) and updates dynamic (10 and 6 years), which had an impact in the quality/ reliability of the results, which can be seen only as approximate.|The objective of EEA was to estimate the likelihood of presence of HNV farmland within Europe using existing European-wide datasets. The CLC European dataset was used as it was available consistently across the great majority of European countries. It was, though, noted that these data have several drawbacks related to geometric limitations (minimum mapping unit [MMU] of 25 ha), thematic resolution (particular class assessment) and updates dynamic (10 and 6 years), which had an impact in the quality/ reliability of the results, which can be seen only as approximate.|The objective of EEA was to estimate the likelihood of presence of HNV farmland within Europe using existing European-wide datasets. The CLC European dataset was used as it was available consistently across the great majority of European countries. It was, though, noted that these data have several drawbacks related to geometric limitations (minimum mapping unit [MMU] of 25 ha), thematic resolution (particular class assessment) and updates dynamic (10 and 6 years), which had an impact in the quality/ reliability of the results, which can be seen only as approximate.|
