Application name

URBAN MORPHOLOGICAL ZONES

Application domain

### EU / international Urban

Responsible organisation / client

EEA 2014

Short description of the application, describing role of CLC

An Urban Morphological Zone can be defined as “A set of built-up areas laying less than 200 m apart”. The data set is used to overcome the heterogeneity when trying to define the outline of an urban area based on administrative or legal criteria. Instead, it uses the concept of connected built-up areas. 

Urban morphological zones (UMZ) are defined by CORINE land cover classes considered to contribute to the urban tissue and function. 

